id: rust.error-context
kind: rust
title: error context across retries
aliases: error context, anyhow context, retryable error, error chain
tags: rust, errors, resilience
questions:
  - when do you attach context to an error, and when do you stop it?
  - how do you keep a retry decision in the error without hiding the original cause?
invariant: An error loses its retry value the moment it drops the context that says where it came from and how many attempts have elapsed.
answer_30s: Attach per-attempt context with anyhow::Context (attempt number, elapsed, remaining budget) but keep the source chain; classify from the inner cause so a transient cause can be retried while an exhausted deadline cannot.
when_to_use:
  - any retry loop that needs to decide retryable vs terminal
  - bridging a library result into an application error with provenance
failure_modes:
  - swallowing the cause with anyhow::anyhow so the original error is gone
  - retrying on the wrong cause because context did not label the attempt
related:
  - rust.anyhow-thiserror
  - rust.retry
sources:
  - https://docs.rs/anyhow/latest/anyhow/trait.Context.html
